"""Derive SkyyEssentials/build_skyyessentials_0.1.14.py from SkyyEssentials 0.1.13 (build_skyyessentials_0.1.13.py, GENERATED by
tools/essentials_0_1_13_patch.py - never edit a generated script, edit this patch). Every anchor is asserted once; at the end every change is
undone on a copy and compared with 0.1.13 (tools/soundpass_gen.Patch). Line endings kept.
Run:  python tools/essentials_0_1_14_patch.py   then   python SkyyEssentials/build_skyyessentials_0.1.14.py   (never --deploy)
Check: python SkyyEssentials/test_skyyessentials_0.1.14.py [--dir <folder inside tools/dev/scratch/>] [--keep] [--only wicon,...]

0.1.14 (2026-10-17) = WARP ICONS (round tp37; docs/answered/world.md 2026-10-17). Skyy: "give players warp. put it in the teleports page
(only admin can set warps. but players can see them, and rearrange them in their teleport menu. (if posible i want a bunch of custom icons we
can set to a warp when making it. for mining fishing foraging farming and what not. probably 1 per zone.)"
  Warps stay VANILLA warps (TeleportPlugin; /warpadmin edits them, SkyyMenu's Teleport page lists them). This version adds the icon.
  1. THE ICON SET = art/warp-icons/manifest.json (read at build): theme ids warp (the signpost = the default), hub, spawn (reused approved
     art/menu-icons-2 pictures) + mining, foraging, farming, fishing, combat, dungeon, boss, shop, portal, cave, home (new, DRAFT art).
     The pictures are SkyyMenu's icon-only items Skyy_Menu_Icon_Warp<Name> (SkyyMenu 0.3.37 ships them; this jar ships no art).
  2. /warpadmin: every warp row has an Icon button (its picture's name); a click opens the PICK view (same hub page): one button per theme,
     4 per row, the current one Primary, each with its picture while SkyyMenu's icon item exists on the server (Item asset map; without
     SkyyMenu the buttons stand alone). A pick saves at once; Cancel keeps it. Add warp here opens the pick view for the new warp at once
     (Cancel = the signpost). Rename carries the icon to the new name, Remove drops it. Each pick is a config-changes.log line
     (warpicon[<id>], via command, like the other warp edits). The row widths shrank to make room (name 280, world 200, position 220,
     made by 170, Icon 140).
  3. SAVED DATA (new file, nothing else touched): Skyy_SkyyEssentials/warpicons.properties - '<warp id lower case>=<theme>' per warp that
     has a pick other than warp; written at once (tmp + fsync + atomic rename, EssStore.replaceFile); an unknown theme / bad line is
     skipped on load (that warp shows the signpost). Read once at start.
  4. BRIDGE (java.lang only): essentials:fn:warps = Function (any argument) -> String[] '<warp id>|<theme>' for every vanilla warp, A-Z
     (theme warp = no pick). Published with the 0.1.13 bridge Functions (EssHFn kind 4) and removed with them.
  No new command, permission, setting or config key. ROLLBACK to 0.1.13: safe (warpicons.properties is ignored; the warps are vanilla's).
"""
